{
  "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1_title",
      "text": "Most hackathon demos are a screen recording and an apology. This template turns a repository into a narrated, subtitled demo video from a single command. This is what that command produces.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "card",
        "template": "title"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2_term",
      "text": "First you write the story: a title, a problem, the product working, and a close. Every segment gets narration, generated locally. Terminal scenes are scripted line by line, so the screen shows exactly what the tool printed.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "term",
        "title": "democut - one command to a finished demo",
        "lines": [
          {
            "at": 0.4,
            "type": "cmd",
            "text": "./scripts/run.sh",
            "cps": 16
          },
          {
            "at": 2.0,
            "text": "[tts]    s1_title    narration   13.8s",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 2.9,
            "text": "[tts]    s2_term     narration   15.6s",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 3.8,
            "text": "[tts]    s3_app      narration   16.3s",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 4.7,
            "text": "[tts]    s4_close    narration   12.8s",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 5.8,
            "type": "rule"
          },
          {
            "at": 6.8,
            "text": "[rec]    card    s1_title     ok",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 7.7,
            "text": "[rec]    term    s2_term      13 lines",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 8.6,
            "text": "[rec]    page    s3_app       7 actions",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 9.5,
            "text": "[rec]    card    s4_close     ok",
            "cls": "dim"
          },
          {
            "at": 10.6,
            "text": "[build]  trim -> concat -> subtitles -> loudnorm",
            "cls": "white"
          },
          {
            "at": 12.0,
            "text": "[qa]     no issues  -  contact sheet rendered",
            "cls": "green"
          },
          {
            "at": 13.4,
            "text": "out/demo.mp4   60.3s   1080p30   ready",
            "cls": "green",
            "flash": "g"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s3_app",
      "text": "Live pages record themselves: scrolls, clicks, typed text, a visible cursor. The build measures every clip against the narration, trims the lead-in, and freezes the last frame when a scene runs short. That is why every segment lands on the beat.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "page",
        "src": "app/index.html",
        "zoom": 1.5,
        "wait_for": [
          "text=Ship with confidence"
        ],
        "actions": [
          {
            "action": "move",
            "x": 0.5,
            "y": 0.12,
            "dur": 0.7
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".stats",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "after": 0.6
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".runs",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "after": 0.5
          },
          {
            "action": "click",
            "sel": "#search",
            "after": 0.3
          },
          {
            "action": "type",
            "sel": "#search",
            "text": "deploy confidence",
            "cps": 16,
            "after": 0.5
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".activity",
            "dur": 1.1,
            "after": 0.7
          },
          {
            "action": "scrollTo",
            "sel": ".cta",
            "dur": 1.2,
            "after": 1.1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s4_close",
      "text": "Then ffmpeg muxes, normalizes loudness, and burns subtitles. One file, ready to upload. Copy this folder into your project, rewrite the story, and ship.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "card",
        "template": "close"
      }
    }
  ]
}
